{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y={e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." 13194139534957 true] [17592186322484 1113 #uuid "60c74d98-62e0-535f-ae2c-bd22a02ff3d1" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322484 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-4x})}^{′}+4(u{e}^{-4x}) & ={e}^{-4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-4u{e}^{-4x}+4u{e}^{-4x} & ={e}^{-4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-\\cancel{4u{e}^{-4x}}+\\cancel{4u{e}^{-4x}} & ={e}^{-4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x} & ={e}^{-4x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-4x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =x{e}^{-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322486 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322487 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322488 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322489 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322490 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1041 "field-1" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322490 13194139534957 true] [17592186322485 1110 #uuid "2f1aa440-de26-5e86-9398-1c01996f574f" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322486 1034 "u(x){e}^{-2x}" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322486 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534957 true] [17592186322486 1111 #uuid "9002d45b-9d8f-578e-a60b-15c24302564d" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322487 1034 "u(x){e}^{-6x}" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534957 true] [17592186322487 1111 #uuid "5022e34b-3eb8-54c0-b8b6-4b67a4472e98" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322488 1034 "u(x){e}^{4x}" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534957 true] [17592186322488 1111 #uuid "29e186fa-1b2c-594c-93e2-0cc194a2133c" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322489 1034 "u(x){e}^{2x}" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322489 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534957 true] [17592186322489 1111 #uuid "5c43d78b-e262-54f3-9558-26c56304fb86" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322490 1034 "u(x){e}^{-4x}" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322490 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534957 true] [17592186322490 1111 #uuid "52d11c94-b79c-59db-88ea-5b09afb3cbce" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322492 13194139534957 true] [17592186322491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322493 13194139534957 true] [17592186322491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322494 13194139534957 true] [17592186322491 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322495 13194