substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-3x})}^{′}+3(u{e}^{-3x}) & =1-4x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-3x}-3u{e}^{-3x}+3u{e}^{-3x} & =1-4x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-3x}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{-3x}}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{-3x}} & =1-4x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-3x} & =1-4x \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{3x}(1-4x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{3x}(1-4x) \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3x}(1-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{3x}(1-4x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-3x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{3x}(1-4x)\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{-3x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\int {e}^{3x}(1-4x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322596 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322597 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322598 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322599 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322600 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1041 "field-1" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322599 13194139534957 true] [17592186322595 1110 #uuid "48a936a0-515e-59af-9108-c2d2d81861cf" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322596 1034 "u(x){e}^{3x}" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534957 true] [17592186322596 1111 #uuid "e592a8d3-17e8-59c7-afe6-4cc9d2c43f5a" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322597 1034 "u(x){e}^{4x}" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534957 true] [17592186322597 1111 #uuid "83aa7265-d0b5-5528-a307-8cf58fe6fe10" 13194139534957 true] [17592186322598 1034 "u(x){e}^{x}" 13194139534957 true] [1759218